 "preferred_specification": {
  "spec": "Q3b_flex_volume",
  "weighting": "ols",
  "justification": "OLS over WLS_n: WLS_n degrades CV for every spec, shifts beta_logn +28-48%, and leaves a +0.32 mean residual for sub-100-rating games (volume leaks into the residual exactly where low-n candidates live); gls_eff ~ OLS shows measurement noise is small vs between-game variance, so n-weighting reweights the population rather than correcting noise. Band-based volume (Q3b) over linear log_n: Part A shows the volume-quality curve is convex and non-monotonic at the bottom; linear control leaves a U-shaped banded residual (max|bandmean| 0.128), bands remove it and add +0.012 CV R2. Categories kept, mechanics as sensitivity (Q3b vs Q4 agreement printed).",
